        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Nile</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">1 to 3 August 1798; the main fighting began at about 18:20 on 1 August</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Aboukir Bay, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, about 20 miles (32 km) north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> under Rear-Admiral Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a>, with 13 ships of the line, and the French Navy under Vice-admiral François-Paul Brueys d'Aigalliers, with 13 ships of the line and four frigates; 17 French ships were engaged</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Brueys was killed and his flagship Orient blew up; only two French ships of the line and two frigates escaped, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army was left in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> without a fleet.</span></div>
        </div>
