    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Brueys anchored his 13 ships of the line in a line inside the bay, but left room between the leading ship and the shoal, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Nelson</a>'s ships passed through it and caught the French vanguard in a crossfire.</li><li>Of 17 French ships engaged, two ships of the line and two frigates escaped; the French flagship Orient blew up at about 22:00 with more than 1,000 men killed.</li><li>The defeat left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army trapped in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> the dominant position in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> that it kept for the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Nelson</a> pursued the French for more than two months and passed their invasion convoy in the dark on 22 June, missing it by less than a day when he reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> on 28 June.</p></aside>
    </section>

